  "result": "Based on my search of the MemPalace memory and documentation, I found the answer.\n\nThe screen specification that covers where an administrator can check outbound webhook notifications to their registered endpoint is **SCR-023 — Webhooks** in the screen specification document.\n\nThis specification defines the page at `/{orgSlug}/settings/webhooks` where administrators can:\n- View their registered webhook endpoints\n- Manage webhook configurations\n- See delivery attempts history (REQ-159: \"Delivery attempts are visible in the settings UI\")\n\nThe specification explicitly states it satisfies REQ-159, which requires delivery attempts to be visible in the settings UI. The `WebhookManager` component handles rendering the endpoint list along with delivery attempt information, allowing administrators to check whether outbound notifications to their registered endpoints went out and what responses came back.\n\nANSWER: docs/ui/screen-settings-billing-flags-webhooks.md",
